{"id": "unknown-2026-11-01-032", "date": "2026-11-01", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 44, "weekday": "Sun"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["ev_penetration", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["expand", "slow"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Eli teases the launch of a much faster electric microcar", "content": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://electrek.co/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2024/05/eli-zero-microcar-header.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Eli Electric Vehicles is getting ready to reveal a new version of its tiny electric microcar, and this one could expand its usefulness beyond the slow lane.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"microcar,nevs\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"490464\" href=\"https://elec", "sources": [{"name": "electrek", "url": "https://electrek.co/2026/11/01/eli-teases-the-launch-of-a-much-faster-electric-microcar/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-01-033", "date": "2026-11-01", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 44, "weekday": "Sun"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Yes, electric motorcycles will replace gasoline motorcycles, but not the way you think", "content": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://electrek.co/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/04/flying-flea-royal-enfield-motorcycle-header.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For years, the conventional wisdom surrounding electric motorcycles has been fairly straightforward: Build an electric motorcycle that’s just as good as a gasoline-powered motorcycle, make it affordable enough, and eventually riders will switch.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It’", "sources": [{"name": "electrek", "url": "https://electrek.co/2026/11/01/yes-electric-motorcycles-will-replace-gasoline-motorcycles-but-not-the-way-you-think/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-01-034", "date": "2026-11-01", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 44, "weekday": "Sun"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Peterbilt makes it easier than ever for government fleets to go electric", "content": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://electrek.co/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/11/PB_EV-Family-Lineup_1_Hi-Res.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Legendary truck brand Peterbilt is lowering procurement barriers for state and municipal fleets looking to electrify their assets by adding its growing lineup of medium- and heavy-duty battery electric trucks to its cooperative purchasing Agreement with Sourcewell.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"pos", "sources": [{"name": "electrek", "url": "https://electrek.co/2026/11/01/peterbilt-makes-it-easier-than-ever-for-government-fleets-to-go-electric/", "type": "rss"}]}
